#+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
# This is an EXUDYN example
#
# Details:  The symbolic system: Notebook `python/Notebooks/tutorialSymbolicSystem.ipynb`. Two mass points hang
#           on spring-dampers under gravity. The system is built with the user items of
#           `exudyn.symbolics.userItems` - the same Create functions as with `mbs` -, recorded, and
#           `SymbolicSystem` gives its equations of motion as expressions, evaluates them and integrates them
#           with the solvers of `exudyn.symbolics.solvers`. The symbolic system is a replicate of `mbs`: its
#           solution is written into `mbs`, so the sensors, the solution file and the solution viewer show it as
#           after `mbs.SolveDynamic`.
#
# Author:   Johannes Gerstmayr
